p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 356)</h2>
<p><b>Detached browsing is truly private, and the Share panel tells the truth.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>On the web, ● LIVE is now synced both ways — scrubbing while live drives the room and you stay live, like a desktop seat. Detaching (the chip) is private browsing: nothing you do moves anyone, nothing moves you, and latching back on snaps you to wherever the room is. Previously a detached seat still drove the app.</li>
<li>The Shared Review panel now shows a web link only when it belongs to the session you're actually hosting — never a leftover from an earlier share — and gains a "Share to the web" section pointing at the no-download browser flow.</li>
<li>Rejoining pages are greeted within two seconds instead of ten — a reload finds the room immediately.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
